{"id": "section-body-01011", "title": "Sepsis and Septic Shock", "chapterId": "chapter-one", "blocks": [{"id": "body-01011", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Sepsis and Septic Shock", "runs": [{"text": "Sepsis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Septic"}, {"text": " Shock"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1890"}}, {"id": "body-01012", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Septicemia (Sepsis) is defined as life-threatening organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to bacterial infection (commonly) and fungal or viral infections. Organ dysfunction can be represented by an increase in the Sequential [Sepsis-related] Organ Failure Assessment (SOFA) score of 2 points or more, with an in-hospital mortality greater than 10%.", "runs": [{"text": "Septicemia (Sepsis) is defined as life-threatening organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to bacterial infection (commonly) and fungal or viral infections. Organ dysfunction can be represented by an increase in the Sequential [Sepsis-related]"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Organ Failure Assessment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(SOFA)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "score of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2 points"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with an in-hospital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mortality"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "greater"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than 10%."}]}, {"id": "body-01013", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Septic Shock is defined as a subset of sepsis in which particularly profound circulatory, cellular, and metabolic abnormalities are associated with a greater risk of mortality than 40%.", "runs": [{"text": "Septic Shock is defined as a subset of sepsis in which particularly profound circulatory, cellular, and metabolic abnormalities are associated with a greater risk of mortality than 40%."}]}, {"id": "body-01014", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-01015", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Temperature of >38oC or <360C; Heart rate of >90/min; Respiratory rate of >20/min or PaCO2 <32 mm Hg", "runs": [{"text": "Temperature"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": ">38oC"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "<360C;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Heart"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": ">90/min;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Respiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": ">20/min"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PaCO2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "<32"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mm"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hg"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1874"}}, {"id": "body-01016", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Above features plus evidence of organ dysfunction (hypotension, jaundice, oliguria, or altered state of consciousness from altered sensorium like drowsiness/lethargy", "runs": [{"text": "Above features plus evidence of organ dysfunction (hypotension, jaundice, oliguria, or altered state of consciousness from altered sensorium like drowsiness/lethargy"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1874"}}, {"id": "body-01017", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigations", "runs": [{"text": "Investigations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-01018", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Blood gases analysis, Bedside ultrasound- assessing the inferior vena cava and the lungs, POC ECG, Urine dipstick, Chest X-ray if suspecting pneumonia, Complete blood count, Qualitative or quantitative CRP or Procalcitonin in centers available, Serum Electrolytes, Creatinine and Urea, Liver function tests- liver enzymes, bilirubin, clotting time, Blood culture and antimicrobial susceptibility testing. Primary source of infection’s clinical sample culture (e.g., urine, pus, sputum CSF etc.) and antimicrobial susceptibility testing and/or RNA/DNA PCR for viral pathogens (where indicated).", "runs": [{"text": "Blood gases analysis, Bedside ultrasound- assessing the inferior vena cava and the lungs, POC ECG, Urine dipstick, Chest X-ray if suspecting pneumonia, Complete blood count, Qualitative or quantitative CRP or Procalcitonin in centers available, Serum Electrolytes, Creatinine and Urea, Liver function tests- liver enzymes, bilirubin, clotting time, Blood culture and antimicrobial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "susceptibility"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "testing."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Primary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "source"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sample"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "culture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "urine,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pus,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sputum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CSF"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "etc.)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and antimicrobial susceptibility testing and/or RNA/DNA PCR for viral pathogens (where indicated)."}]}, {"id": "body-01020", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Diagnostic criteria", "runs": [{"text": "Diagnostic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "criteria"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-01021", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Sepsis: Q-SOFA in settings with limited laboratory infrastructures: two or more SOFA scores, namely: Respiratory rate", "runs": [{"text": "Sepsis:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Q-SOFA"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "settings"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "limited"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infrastructures:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "two"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "SOFA"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "scores,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "namely:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Respiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rate"}]}, {"id": "body-01022", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "≥22/min, altered mentation, and Systolic blood pressure ≥100 mm Hg) ± bacteria or fungal proven blood culture and susceptibility testing are recommended to make a definitive diagnosis.", "runs": [{"text": "≥22/min,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "altered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mentation,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Systolic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pressure"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "≥100"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mm"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hg)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "±"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bacteria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fungal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "proven"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "culture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and susceptibility testing are recommended to make a definitive diagnosis."}]}, {"id": "body-01023", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Other scoring criteria include SOFA, NEWS (National Early Warning Score), and MEDS (Mortality in Emergency Medicine Department Sepsis", "runs": [{"text": "Other scoring criteria include SOFA, NEWS (National Early Warning Score), and MEDS (Mortality in Emergency Medicine Department Sepsis"}]}, {"id": "body-01024", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Septic shock: Sepsis diagnostic criteria above and vasopressor therapy needed to elevate MAP ≥65 mmHg and lactate >2 mmol/L (18 mg/dL) despite adequate fluid resuscitation.", "runs": [{"text": "Septic shock: Sepsis diagnostic criteria above and vasopressor therapy needed to elevate MAP ≥65 mmHg and lactate >2 mmol/L (18 mg/dL) despite adequate fluid resuscitation."}]}, {"id": "body-01025", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-01026", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Nutritional support", "runs": [{"text": "Nutritional"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "support"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1874"}}, {"id": "body-01027", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Control measures focused on the primary focus of infection.", "runs": [{"text": "Control"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "measures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "focused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "focus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1874"}}, {"id": "body-01028", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Perform primary and secondary assessment and provide necessary interventions", "runs": [{"text": "Perform"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "primary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "secondary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "assessment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "provide"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "necessary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "interventions"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1874"}}, {"id": "body-01029", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Ensure patency of the airway and give oxygen if hypoxic or increased work of breathing", "runs": [{"text": "Ensure"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "airway"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "give"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oxygen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hypoxic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increased"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "work"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "breathing"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1874"}}, {"id": "body-01030", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Connect the patient to the cardiac monitor and obtain vital signs", "runs": [{"text": "Connect"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monitor"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "obtain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1874"}}, {"id": "body-01032", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-01034", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: sodium chloride 0.9% (IV) Adults: 2litres; Paediatrics: 20mls/kg.", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "sodium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chloride"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "0.9%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Adults:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2litres;"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Paediatrics:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "20mls/kg."}]}, {"id": "body-01035", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-01036", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: sodium lactate compound (ringer’s lactate)(IV): Adults 2litres; Paediatrics 20mls/kg in 20 minutes as a first bolus followed by a second bolus of 2litres/20mls/kg (use small boluses in CCF).", "runs": [{"text": "A: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "sodium lactate compound (ringer’s lactate)(IV): Adults 2litres; Paediatrics 20mls/kg in 20 minutes as a first bolus followed by a second bolus of 2litres/20mls/kg (use small boluses in CCF)."}]}, {"id": "body-01037", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-01038", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: dobutamine (IV) 2-20mcg/kg/min can be given for patients in shock not responding to fluids or when there is poor cardiac output.", "runs": [{"text": "S: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "dobutamine (IV) 2-20mcg/kg/min can be given for patients in shock not responding to fluids or when there is poor cardiac output."}]}, {"id": "body-01039", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-01040", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: norepinephrine (IV) 5-20mcg/min for patients in septic shock not responding after the first 30mls/kg of IVF bolus to maintain the mean arterial pressure (MAP) of ≥ 65mm Hg", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "norepinephrine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5-20mcg/min"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "septic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "shock"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "responding"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "first"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "30mls/kg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "IVF"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bolus to maintain the mean arterial pressure (MAP) of ≥ 65mm Hg"}]}, {"id": "body-01041", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "AND", "runs": [{"text": "AND"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-01042", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: hydrocortisone (IV) 200mg stat.", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "hydrocortisone"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "200mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stat."}]}, {"id": "body-01043", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-01044", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: albumin 60g of 20% running for 2-3 hours", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "albumin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "60g"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "20%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "running"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2-3"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hours"}]}, {"id": "body-01045-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note:", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-01045-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Transfuse blood (If hemoglobin is < 7g/dl)", "runs": [{"text": "Transfuse"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(If"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hemoglobin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "<"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7g/dl)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1876"}}, {"id": "body-01045-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Lactate clearance should be used as a resuscitation target.", "runs": [{"text": "Lactate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clearance"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "used"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "resuscitation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "target."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1876"}}, {"id": "body-01046", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Antimicrobial therapies (broad-spectrum antibiotics must be started within the first hour):", "runs": [{"text": "Antimicrobial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapies"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(broad-spectrum"}, {"t